### Problem:
You are tasked with creating a custom annotation processor in Java. Your annotation, `ConstructorAnno`, is used to mark constructors in classes. The annotation takes a single optional parameter, `value`, which defaults to "default".

Your goal is to implement a processor that, when given a class with constructors annotated with `ConstructorAnno`, generates a report listing the constructors and their corresponding values.

Your annotation should be defined as follows:
```java
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Target({ElementType.CONSTRUCTOR})
@Inherited
public @interface ConstructorAnno {
    String value() default "default";
}
```

Your processor should generate a report in the following format:
```
Class: <class name>
Constructor: <constructor signature>, Value: <value>
```
For example:
```
Class: MyClass
Constructor: MyClass(int), Value: custom
Constructor: MyClass(), Value: default
```

Write a custom annotation processor that accomplishes this task.

### Solution:
```java
import javax.annotation.processing.*;
import javax.lang.model.SourceVersion;
import javax.lang.model.element.*;
import javax.tools.Diagnostic;
import java.util.Set;

@SupportedAnnotationTypes("ConstructorAnno")
@SupportedSourceVersion(SourceVersion.RELEASE_8)
public class ConstructorAnnoProcessor extends AbstractProcessor {

    @Override
    public boolean process(Set<? extends TypeElement> annotations, RoundEnvironment roundEnv) {
        for (Element element : roundEnv.getElementsAnnotatedWith(ConstructorAnno.class)) {
            if (element.getKind() == ElementKind.CONSTRUCTOR) {
                String className = ((TypeElement) element.getEnclosingElement()).getQualifiedName().toString();
                String constructorSignature = element.asType().toString();
                String value = element.getAnnotation(ConstructorAnno.class).value();
                processingEnv.getMessager().printMessage(Diagnostic.Kind.NOTE, "Class: " + className + "\nConstructor: " + constructorSignature + ", Value: " + value);
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

This processor uses the `javax.annotation.processing` package to process the `ConstructorAnno` annotation. It iterates through the elements annotated with `ConstructorAnno`, extracts the class name, constructor signature, and value, and then prints a report using the `Messager` provided by the processing environment.

