/**
 * @author <a href="mailto:john.doe@example.com">John Doe</a>
 */
```

Your task is to write a Java program that reads the given source code snippet and extracts the author's name and email address. You should then store this information in a suitable data structure for further processing.

Write a Java program that accomplishes the following:
1. Parses the given source code snippet to extract the author's name and email address.
2. Stores the extracted information in a data structure for further processing.
3. Outputs the stored information in a readable format.

Ensure that your program handles different variations of the author's name and email address format that may appear in the source code comments.

### Solution:
```java
import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class AuthorExtractor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sourceCode = "...\n" +
                " * @author <a href=\"mailto:john.doe@example.com\">John Doe</a>\n" +
                " */";

        Map<String, String> authorMap = extractAuthorInfo(sourceCode);
        for (Map.Entry<String, String> entry : authorMap.entrySet()) {
            System.out.println("Author: " + entry.getKey() + ", Email: " + entry.getValue());
        }
    }

    public static Map<String, String> extractAuthorInfo(String sourceCode) {
        Map<String, String> authorMap = new HashMap<>();
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile("@author <a href=\"mailto:(.*?)\">(.*?)</a>");
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(sourceCode);

        while (matcher.find()) {
            String email = matcher.group(1);
            String name = matcher.group(2);
            authorMap.put(name, email);
        }

        return authorMap;
    }
}
```

