import org.apache.zookeeper.CreateMode;
import org.apache.zookeeper.data.Stat;

public class ZooKeeperDemo {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        String connectionString = "localhost:2181"; // Replace with the actual ZooKeeper server connection string
        String znodePath = "/myZnode";
        byte[] znodeData = "Hello, ZooKeeper!".getBytes();

        // Create a CuratorFramework instance to connect to the ZooKeeper server
        CuratorFramework client = CuratorFrameworkFactory.newClient(connectionString, new ExponentialBackoffRetry(1000, 3));
        client.start();

        // Create the znode with the specified path and data
        client.create().creatingParentsIfNeeded().withMode(CreateMode.PERSISTENT).forPath(znodePath, znodeData);

        // Retrieve the data from the created znode
        Stat stat = new Stat();
        byte[] retrievedData = client.getData().storingStatIn(stat).forPath(znodePath);

        // Display the retrieved data
        System.out.println("Retrieved data from znode " + znodePath + ": " + new String(retrievedData));

        // Close the CuratorFramework client
        client.close();
    }
}
```

In this solution, we create a Java program that connects to a ZooKeeper server using the Curator framework, creates a znode with some data, retrieves the data from the znode, and displays it. The program uses the provided code snippet as a starting point and incorporates the necessary logic to achieve the described functionality.

