You are tasked with implementing a function that filters a collection of art pieces based on various criteria. The function should take in a list of art pieces, each represented by a structure containing the following fields:

- `categoryId` (integer): The category ID of the art piece.
- `from` (string): The starting date of the art piece's creation.
- `to` (string): The ending date of the art piece's creation.
- `title` (string): The title of the art piece.
- `artistId` (integer, optional, default: 0): The ID of the artist who created the art piece.
- `styleId` (integer, optional, default: 0): The ID representing the style of the art piece.

You need to implement a function `filterArtPieces` that takes in the list of art pieces and the following filter criteria:

- `categoryIds` (array of integers): The category IDs to include in the filtered result.
- `fromDate` (string): The starting date for filtering the art pieces.
- `toDate` (string): The ending date for filtering the art pieces.
- `artistId` (integer, optional, default: 0): The ID of the artist to include in the filtered result.
- `styleId` (integer, optional, default: 0): The ID representing the style to include in the filtered result.

The function should return a new list containing only the art pieces that satisfy all the provided filter criteria.

You need to implement the `filterArtPieces` function.

Function Signature: `List<ArtPiece> filterArtPieces(List<ArtPiece> artPieces, int[] categoryIds, string fromDate, string toDate, int artistId = 0, int styleId = 0)`

Example:
Suppose we have the following art pieces:
```
ArtPiece 1: {categoryId: 1, from: "2020-01-01", to: "2020-12-31", title: "Sunset", artistId: 101, styleId: 201}
ArtPiece 2: {categoryId: 2, from: "2019-06-15", to: "2020-06-14", title: "Starry Night", artistId: 102, styleId: 202}
ArtPiece 3: {categoryId: 1, from: "2021-03-20", to: "2021-09-20", title: "Morning Dew", artistId: 101, styleId: 203}
```

If we call `filterArtPieces([ArtPiece1, ArtPiece2, ArtPiece3], [1], "2020-01-01", "2021-12-31", 0, 0)`, the output should be `[ArtPiece1, ArtPiece3]` as only these two art pieces belong to category 1 and fall within the specified date range.

### Solution:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

class ArtPiece {
    int categoryId;
    String from;
    String to;
    String title;
    int artistId;
    int styleId;

    public ArtPiece(int categoryId, String from, String to, String title, int artistId, int styleId) {
        this.categoryId = categoryId;
        this.from = from;
        this.to = to;
        this.title = title;
        this.artistId = artistId;
        this.styleId = styleId;
    }
}

public class ArtPieceFilter {
    public List<ArtPiece> filterArtPieces(List<ArtPiece> artPieces, int[] categoryIds, String fromDate, String toDate, int artistId, int styleId) {
        List<ArtPiece> filteredArtPieces = new ArrayList<>();
        for (ArtPiece artPiece : artPieces) {
            if (isArtPieceValid(artPiece, categoryIds, fromDate, toDate, artistId, styleId)) {
                filteredArtPieces.add(artPiece);
            }
        }
        return filteredArtPieces;
    }

    private boolean isArtPieceValid(ArtPiece artPiece, int[] categoryIds, String fromDate, String toDate, int artistId, int styleId) {
        if (artistId != 0 && artPiece.artistId != artistId) {
            return false;
        }
        if (styleId != 0 && artPiece.styleId != styleId) {
            return false;
        }
        if (!isInCategoryIds(artPiece.categoryId, categoryIds)) {
            return false;
        }
        if (artPiece.from.compareTo(fromDate) < 0 || artPiece.to.compareTo(toDate) > 0) {
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }

    private boolean isInCategoryIds(int categoryId, int[] categoryIds) {
        for (int id : categoryIds) {
            if (categoryId == id) {
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArtPiece artPiece1 = new ArtPiece(1, "2020-01-01", "2020-12-31", "Sunset", 101, 201);
        ArtPiece artPiece2 = new ArtPiece(2, "2019-06-15", "2020-06-14", "Starry Night", 102, 202);
        ArtPiece artPiece3 = new ArtPiece(1, "2021-03-20", "2021-09-20", "Morning Dew", 101, 203);

        List<ArtPiece> artPieces = new ArrayList<>();
        artPieces.add(artPiece1);
        artPieces.add(artPiece2);
        artPieces.add(artPiece3);

        ArtPieceFilter artPieceFilter = new ArtPieceFilter();
        List<ArtPiece> filteredArtPieces = artPieceFilter.filterArtPieces(artPieces, new int[]{1}, "2020-01-01", "2021-12-31", 0, 0);

        for (ArtPiece artPiece : filteredArtPieces) {
            System.out.println(artPiece.title);
        }
    }
}
```

