You are tasked with creating a notification management system for a web application. The system should allow users to push notifications and clear all notifications. Additionally, there should be a theme toggle feature to switch between light and dark themes. You are provided with a code snippet that includes a navigation bar with buttons for pushing notifications, clearing all notifications, and toggling the theme.

Your task is to implement the notification management system and the theme toggle feature using React. You should create the necessary components and functions to handle the notification actions and theme toggling. The notification system should support adding new notifications, clearing all notifications, and displaying the notifications in the user interface. The theme toggle should switch between light and dark themes, updating the appearance of the application accordingly.

You should use React and any additional libraries or tools as needed to accomplish the task. Ensure that the components are responsive and provide a smooth user experience.

Implement the notification management system and theme toggle feature using React.

### Solution:
```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';

// Notification component
const Notification = ({ message, dismissNotification }) => {
  return (
    <div className="notification">
      <span>{message}</span>
      <button onClick={dismissNotification}>Dismiss</button>
    </div>
  );
};

// NotificationManager component
const NotificationManager = () => {
  const [notifications, setNotifications] = useState([]);

  const pushNotification = (message) => {
    setNotifications([...notifications, message]);
  };

  const dismissAllNotifications = () => {
    setNotifications([]);
  };

  const dismissNotification = (index) => {
    const updatedNotifications = [...notifications];
    updatedNotifications.splice(index, 1);
    setNotifications(updatedNotifications);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={() => pushNotification('New notification')}>
        Push a notification
      </button>
      <button onClick={dismissAllNotifications}>
        Clear all notifications
      </button>
      <div className="notifications">
        {notifications.map((message, index) => (
          <Notification
            key={index}
            message={message}
            dismissNotification={() => dismissNotification(index)}
          />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

// ThemeToggle component
const ThemeToggle = () => {
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState('light');

  const toggleTheme = () => {
    setTheme(theme === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light');
    // Apply theme changes to the application
    document.body.classList.toggle('dark-theme');
  };

  return (
    <button onClick={toggleTheme}>
      {theme === 'light' ? 'Switch to Dark Theme' : 'Switch to Light Theme'}
    </button>
  );
};

// App component
const App = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      <nav>
        <NotificationManager />
        <div className="theme-toggle">
          <ThemeToggle />
        </div>
      </nav>
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```

In the solution, we have created three components: `Notification`, `NotificationManager`, and `ThemeToggle`. The `Notification` component handles individual notifications and their dismissal. The `NotificationManager` component manages the state of notifications and provides functionality to push new notifications and clear all notifications. The `ThemeToggle` component handles the theme switching functionality. The `App` component integrates these components into the application's navigation bar. The solution uses React hooks to manage state and handle user interactions. Additionally, it applies the dark theme by toggling the `dark-theme` class on the `body` element.

