You are tasked with implementing a module loader for a JavaScript application. The module loader should be able to import and export modules using the ES6 module syntax. Your task is to create a function that parses the given code snippet and extracts the module names and their corresponding file paths.

Write a function `parseModuleImports` that takes a string representing the code snippet as input and returns an object containing the module names and their file paths. The code snippet will consist of multiple lines, each containing an export statement in the format `export { ModuleName } from 'module/path.js';`.

Your function should extract the module names and their corresponding file paths and return them in an object format. If a module name is already present in the object, the file path should be appended to an array under that module name.

For example, given the following code snippet:
```
export { TiffEndian } from './tiff.endian.js';
export { TiffCompression, TiffMimeType } from './tiff.mime.js';
export { TiffTag, TiffTagGeo } from './tiff.tag.id.js';
export { TiffTagValueType } from './tiff.tag.value.js';
export { TiffVersion } from './tiff.version.js';
```
The function should return the following object:
```javascript
{
  TiffEndian: ['./tiff.endian.js'],
  TiffCompression: ['./tiff.mime.js'],
  TiffMimeType: ['./tiff.mime.js'],
  TiffTag: ['./tiff.tag.id.js'],
  TiffTagGeo: ['./tiff.tag.id.js'],
  TiffTagValueType: ['./tiff.tag.value.js'],
  TiffVersion: ['./tiff.version.js']
}
```

### Solution:
```javascript
function parseModuleImports(codeSnippet) {
  const moduleImports = {};
  const exportStatements = codeSnippet.split('\n');

  for (const statement of exportStatements) {
    const match = statement.match(/export { (.*) } from '(.*)';/);
    if (match) {
      const modules = match[1].split(', ');
      const filePath = match[2];

      modules.forEach(module => {
        const moduleName = module.trim();
        if (moduleImports[moduleName]) {
          moduleImports[moduleName].push(filePath);
        } else {
          moduleImports[moduleName] = [filePath];
        }
      });
    }
  }

  return moduleImports;
}

// Test the function with the provided code snippet
const codeSnippet = `
export { TiffEndian } from './tiff.endian.js';
export { TiffCompression, TiffMimeType } from './tiff.mime.js';
export { TiffTag, TiffTagGeo } from './tiff.tag.id.js';
export { TiffTagValueType } from './tiff.tag.value.js';
export { TiffVersion } from './tiff.version.js';
`;

console.log(parseModuleImports(codeSnippet));
```

The `parseModuleImports` function splits the code snippet into individual export statements and uses regular expressions to extract the module names and file paths. It then populates the `moduleImports` object with the extracted information, handling cases where multiple modules are exported from the same file. Finally, it returns the object containing the module names and their corresponding file paths.

